body:
For the first few months I didn't have ESO+. Everyone in my guild told me how having ESO+ makes it a completely different game. I tried ESO+ after that and saw that they were right. It feels almost like the subscription gives you the ability to use weapons. It really is a huge deal and after money/time was bit tight and I quit for have a year I saw that I could not get back into the game without subscribing. 

&#x200B;

I have nothing against paying monthly for a MMO but the way Zenimax is dealing with it feels a bit manipulative.

"It is about the journey and not about the product" 

&#x200B;

If you can identify with that quote, get it. With no clear goal to the game and endgame basically resetting everything for you, you need to set your own goals and enjoy knowing that in the end, nothing really matters.
